# <%~ it.instance.slug %>: As-built
<%
  /* Intentional consolidation (WI #269, carried into WI #318 / design v2): this
     template deliberately collapses the ATLAS reference's deep Data Migration
     Flows and Migration Services hierarchies (~70 headings) into a few generic
     as-built fields — it is NOT a 1:1 heading map to the reference, and that is
     by design. See docs/research/design-definition-reference-reconciliation.md
     §4 and §9, grounded in docs/reconciliation/as-built-reconciliation.md.
     WI #318: governance sections (`changes-from-design`, `acceptance-criteria`,
     `handover-confirmation`) move to the very end, after the Appendix, matching
     the ATLAS reference's own structure — v1's `requires` order placed them
     between infrastructure and the recovery plan. `nfrs.disaster-recovery-and-
     backup` now renders immediately before the recovery plan it was built to
     meet, and owns RTO/RPO outright. The introduction-section overview is
     renamed "As-built overview" in the As-built design section (v1 repeated
     "## Overview" verbatim in both sections); infrastructure now nests under
     "# As-built design" as a `##` sibling of the other as-built-notes fields
     (v1 gave it its own bare top-level `#`). Blank-field guard `na()` is
     injected once as an Eta functionHeader by lib/render.js (WI #273 / R2). A
     `module.field?` requires entry is in scope but not gate-blocking (WI #276),
     so it renders as a suppress-when-blank `<% if %>` section. WI #331:
     already the cleanest case of the four stages — the framing (required) and
     conditions (optional) fields were already adjacent under one
     "# Introduction" heading, so the position is unchanged; the heading
     splits into "# Overview" (required fields) and "# Design basis" (optional
     fields, still via a shared partial — `_introductionOptional.md.tmpl`
     reworked into `_designBasisOptional.md.tmpl`), both still 2nd/3rd. */
  const intro = it.modules.introduction || {}
  const designBasis = it.modules['design-basis'] || {}
  const glossary = it.modules.glossary || {}
  const notes = it.modules['as-built-notes'] || {}
  const recovery = it.modules['recovery-plan'] || {}
  const dsc = it.modules['data-security-controls'] || {}
%>
